Patch 59: Direct3D 11 renderer for the native GS (Windows), selected with PS2X_GS_BACKEND=d3d11 (default stays OpenGL).
New GSHwD3D11Backend (gs_hw_d3d11.cpp/.h): the same render-target design as GSHwBackend (scaled RGBA targets, PS2 draws as
triangles/sprites/lines, shader-side texture decode, CLUT, depth, alpha/dual-source blend, 16-bit shuffles, composed read
circuits) on D3D11 feature level 11.0 + HLSL 5.0 compiled at run time with d3dcompiler_47.dll (no SDK dependency beyond
d3d11). The frame is read back to the host as RGBA (UsesSharedPresentation() is false), so it shares the host path of the
non-shared OpenGL mode. If no device or compiler exists, Probe() fails and MakeDefault() falls back to OpenGL.
Debug aids: GOW_GS_D3D11_DEBUG=1 (D3D11 debug layer messages after each present), GOW_GS_D3D11_WARP=1 (software WARP device, CI tests only), GOW_GS_HW_STATS=1, PS2X_GS_HW_SCALE.
Not in this backend yet: PCSX2 texture packs (patch 52) and the GL-only shared presentation. Test without the game:
tools/test/d3d11_backend_test.cpp. Origin: this project, modelled on the Tenkaichi3Decomp renderer split (gs_d3d11.cpp).

